    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0102" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1937v05/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/751c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Honduran Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Lozano
                        H</hi>.)<anchor n="46" xml:id="d99-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-10-21">October 21, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Government of the United States in association with the Governments of Costa
                    Rica and Venezuela is glad to tender its good offices to the Governments of
                    Honduras and Nicaragua with the hope that this friendly service may facilitate a
                    pacific solution of the boundary controversy which has unfortunately arisen
                    between the two Republics.</p>
                <p>Should the Republics of Honduras and Nicaragua be disposed to accept this tender
                    of good offices, the three Governments will be happy to offer suggestions for
                    the alleviation of the present tension in the relations between the Republics of
                    Honduras and Nicaragua, and, once that result is accomplished, to make
                    suggestions as to means, equally acceptable to both parties, which might be
                    adopted by Honduras and Nicaragua with the object of reaching a definitive
                    settlement of the controversy.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d99-f1" n="46" type="source" xml:id="d99-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, October 21, to the
                    Nicaraguan Minister for Foreign Affairs, Cordero Reyes.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
